IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc22-jury-defects`

-- ccc22-tests-jury-defects.l4 -- tests for ccc22-jury-defects.l4 (sections 670 to 672). Expected values are written from the text, beside the assertion. Arguments are in the order of each function's GIVEN lines.

§ `Sections 670 to 672`

-- 670: args: a verdict has been returned on an indictment, the ground.
#ASSERT `s 670 the section bars staying or reversing the judgment on the ground` TRUE `s 670(a) an irregularity in the summoning or empanelling of the jury` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 670 the section bars staying or reversing the judgment on the ground` TRUE `s 670(b) that a person who served on the jury was not returned as a juror by a sheriff or other officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 670 the section bars staying or reversing the judgment on the ground` TRUE `s 670 some other ground` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the list is not closed
#ASSERT `s 670 the section bars staying or reversing the judgment on the ground` FALSE `s 670(a) an irregularity in the summoning or empanelling of the jury` EQUALS NOTHING   -- before verdict: the section speaks of judgment "after verdict on an indictment"
-- 671: args: there is an omission to observe directions contained in an Act, the directions, the verdict was rendered in criminal proceedings.
#ASSERT `s 671 the section bars treating the omission as a ground for impeaching or quashing the verdict` TRUE `s 671 the qualification of jurors` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 671 the section bars treating the omission as a ground for impeaching or quashing the verdict` TRUE `s 671 the selection of jurors` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 671 the section bars treating the omission as a ground for impeaching or quashing the verdict` TRUE `s 671 the balloting of jurors` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 671 the section bars treating the omission as a ground for impeaching or quashing the verdict` TRUE `s 671 the distribution of jurors` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 671 the section bars treating the omission as a ground for impeaching or quashing the verdict` TRUE `s 671 the preparation of the jurors’ book` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 671 the section bars treating the omission as a ground for impeaching or quashing the verdict` TRUE `s 671 the selecting of jury lists` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 671 the section bars treating the omission as a ground for impeaching or quashing the verdict` TRUE `s 671 the drafting of panels from the jury lists` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 671 the section bars treating the omission as a ground for impeaching or quashing the verdict` TRUE `s 671 some other directions` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the list is not closed
#ASSERT `s 671 the section bars treating the omission as a ground for impeaching or quashing the verdict` FALSE `s 671 the selection of jurors` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no omission
#ASSERT `s 671 the section bars treating the omission as a ground for impeaching or quashing the verdict` TRUE `s 671 the selection of jurors` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a verdict rendered in criminal proceedings
-- 672 date: the moment immediately before April 1, 1955 is the end of 31 March 1955.
#ASSERT `s 672 the power, authority, practice or form existed immediately before April 1, 1955` (Date 31 3 1955) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672 the power, authority, practice or form existed immediately before April 1, 1955` (Date 30 3 1955) EQUALS NOTHING   -- one day earlier: not the moment named
#ASSERT `s 672 the power, authority, practice or form existed immediately before April 1, 1955` (Date 1 4 1955) EQUALS NOTHING   -- April 1 itself is not "immediately before"
-- 672 saving: args: the power etc. existed immediately before April 1, 1955, it is with respect to trials by jury etc., it is expressly altered by or inconsistent with this Act.
#ASSERT `s 672 the Act leaves the power, authority, practice or form unaltered` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672 the Act leaves the power, authority, practice or form unaltered` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "except where ... expressly altered by or is inconsistent with this Act"
#ASSERT `s 672 the Act leaves the power, authority, practice or form unaltered` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in existence immediately before April 1, 1955
#ASSERT `s 672 the Act leaves the power, authority, practice or form unaltered` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not with respect to trials by jury, jury process, juries or jurors
